  <RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.InvalidSelection>无效的存档选择</RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.InvalidSelection>
  <RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.NeedName>需要为存档文件输入名称</RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.NeedName>
  <RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.CannotDeleteCreateNew>无法删除存档名称行</RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.CannotDeleteCreateNew>
  <!-- {0} = file name (stripped of extension). -->
  <!-- Row LABELS only (element-uniformity campaign, task 8 packet E). These
       used to be whole-row templates carrying the date and the position too;
       FileListScope now fills an ElementDescription instead, so the composer
       supplies the position and the date-time rides Extras. The mode verb stays
       in the label because it is the only thing distinguishing a save row (Enter
       overwrites) from a load row (Enter loads) once you are inside the list.
       CreateNewLabel takes no argument: the typed name is the row's VALUE.
       Overwrite/Load: {0} = file name, stripped of its extension. -->
  <RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.OverwriteLabel>覆盖：{0}</RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.OverwriteLabel>
  <RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.LoadLabel>载入：{0}</RimWorldAccess.UI.Save.LoadLabel>

  <!-- =================================================================
       Float menu (WindowlessFloatMenuState). The selection announcement
       differentiates between a queued action (Shift held while clicking
       a colonist order) and a normal one. {0} = option label.
       The no-active-search focus announcement (label, disabled state,
       tooltip, position) now renders through AnnouncementComposer.ComposeFocus
       (element-uniformity campaign, task 8 packet B) instead of a hand-built
       key (see WindowlessFloatMenuState.ComposeOptionFocus). The keys below
       remain for the ExecuteSelected rejection message, the active-typeahead-
       search announcement (a shape the composer's fixed fragment order can't
       reproduce), and the search-tooltip variant.
       ================================================================= -->
